+ *   `gl.texElementImage2D`. Each frame we also set the form's CSS transform to
+ *   the exact same projection used to draw the face, so pointer hit-testing,
+ *   focus rings, text selection, etc. land on what the user actually sees.
+ *
+ * Fallback path (browsers without HTML-in-Canvas):
+ *   The form is moved out of the canvas into the stage and overlaid on the
+ *   WebGL box using the same matrix3d projection, so it still looks and
+ *   behaves as if printed on the rotating box.
